title: Authorizations › New case › Sites and scope
route: /authorizations/new (the site switcher in the top bar decides what is in view)
intro: A clinic can run more than one site, and staff at one site must not see the other site's patients. New case follows the sites in view everywhere: the incoming referrals, the patient search, the duplicate check, the site a new case belongs to, and every link. A record at a site the viewer cannot see is never named, counted or searched; a link to it shows 'not available' and nothing else.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: Jordan Perez sees Both sites, Dr. Rivera sees Site A, Sam Okafor sees Site B. Choose the viewer in the Demo menu. A case id decides its site, so a new case gets an id that falls at the site it was made for.
---
start s1 "The viewer and the site switcher\nTop bar: 'Both sites', 'Site A' or 'Site B'\nA viewer limited to one site has nothing to switch"
decision d1 "How many sites are in view?"
process pOne "One site\nEverything below shows that site only\nNothing says how many records are at the other site"
process pBoth "Both sites\nEverything shows both, and each row can name its site"

group gLists "What shows in New case"
  screen l1 "'Incoming referrals (N)'\nOnly open referrals at the sites in view\nThe sidebar badge on 'New case' counts the same ones"
  screen l2 "Patient search\n'Searches Site A only.'\n'No patient at Site A matches “Q.Z.”.' when the match is at the other site\nWith both sites in view each row names its site"
  screen l3 "Possible duplicate\nOnly requests, drafts and authorizations at the sites in view are compared"
  screen l4 "Eligibility & Benefits and Review & submit\nThe verification and the case belong to the case's site"
endgroup

group gSite "The site a new case belongs to"
  decision dLock "Does the case have an id or a patient yet?"
  screen sPick "Both sites in view: a 'Site' choice, Site A or Site B\n'A new patient belongs to one site. Staff at the other site will not see this case.'"
  click cSite "Pick a site"
  process pOneSite "One site in view: 'Site A · this case is at the site you are working at.'"
  process pLocked "Locked\nWith a patient: 'the patient's site'\nWith an id: 'set when the case got its ID'"
  store stId "The case id is chosen so that it falls at the site\nR- for Residential 3.5 and Detox, I- for IOP, P- for PHP"
  process pRef "A referral read from dropped files is placed at the site in view\nIts RF number is the next one that falls there"
  process pNarrow "Narrowing the view while a blank case is open\nThe case moves to the site in view\nA case with an id or a patient stays where it is"
endgroup

group gLinks "A link to a record at a site that is not in view"
  decision dLink "What does the link open?"
  screen o1 "A referral: ?referral=RF-2045 or the full referral page\n'This referral is not available at Site A'"
  screen o2 "A case being prepared: /authorizations/new/draft-ID\n'This case is not available at Site A'"
  process o3 "?patient= and ?verification= from the other site are ignored\nA blank case opens instead"
  process o4 "Picking a patient from a stale list does nothing\nThe other site's patient cannot be brought in"
  decision dWho "Can the viewer see both sites?"
  screen sShow "One-site viewer: 'RF-2045 belongs to Site B. Dr. Rivera can see Site A only. Access follows the site, so staff see only the patients they work with.'\nNo patient, payer or date"
  click cShow "Click 'Show Site B'"
  process pShow "The view switches to that site and the record opens"
endgroup
goto gStart "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Intake › Start with a referral or patient"
goto gFind "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Intake › Find a patient and the authorization"
goto gDup "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Intake › Possible duplicate"
goto gShell "Continues in: Global shell › Top bar › Site switcher"

s1 --> d1
d1 -->|One| pOne --> l1
d1 -->|Both| pBoth --> l1
l1 --> l2 --> l3 --> l4
l1 -.-> gStart
l2 -.-> gFind
l3 -.-> gDup
s1 -.-> gShell
pBoth --> dLock
pOne --> dLock
dLock -->|No, both sites in view| sPick --> cSite --> stId
dLock -->|No, one site in view| pOneSite --> stId
dLock -->|Yes| pLocked
stId --> pRef
stId --> pNarrow
s1 --> dLink
dLink -->|A referral| o1 --> dWho
dLink -->|A case| o2 --> dWho
dLink -->|A patient or a verification| o3
dLink -->|A patient in the list| o4
dWho -->|No| sShow
dWho -->|Yes| cShow --> pShow
